# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Dependencies, build output, logs
node_modules/
ui/dist/
*.log

# The facilitator serves the UI from `//go:embed all:dist`. The tiny
# index.html stub in that directory is TRACKED on purpose — the embed
# fails to compile if the directory has no files, so a plain `go build`
# outside Docker needs it. The real Vite output is copied over it at image
# build time (facilitator/Dockerfile), and none of that may be committed.
# If you ever build locally into this path, check the stub back out before
# committing: .gitignore cannot protect a file that is already tracked.
facilitator/internal/web/dist/*
!facilitator/internal/web/dist/index.html

# Runtime state: volumes, and the active-bank pointer the conductor owns
# after first boot.
shared/

# Secrets. Nothing here needs one today; this is so nothing arrives by
# accident once the repo is public.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Third-party exam dumps used as a topic map while authoring banks. These
# are someone else's copyrighted material; the banks in this repo are
# CC BY-SA 4.0 and must be ours to license, so no dump may ever be
# committed here — not even "temporarily".
killer-sh-*.txt
*-dump.txt

# Local agent/tool state.
#
# Until now these were invisible only because of ~/.config/git/ignore and
# .git/info/exclude — a machine-global file and a repo-local one, neither
# of which survives a clone. Anyone else cloning this repo would have seen
# every one of them as untracked. Listing them here is what makes a fresh
# clone behave the way this working copy already does.
# The .impeccable patterns are unanchored on purpose: ui/ has its own
# .impeccable directory, and root-anchored patterns left its cache file
# visible on a fresh clone.
.claude/settings.local.json
**/.impeccable/config.local.json
**/.impeccable/hook.cache.json
**/.impeccable/hook.pending.json
**/.impeccable/live/sessions/
.superpowers/

# Deliberately NOT ignored, because they are project artifacts rather than
# machine state, and a collaborator needs them to get the same results:
#   .impeccable/design.json      — the DESIGN.md token/component sidecar
#   .impeccable/live/config.json — which HTML file live mode injects into
#   .claude/settings.json        — shared project config, if one is added
